    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8eaebf89",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The loudest one in the room is mapped onto Denzel Washington",
      "description": "The text 'the loudest one in the room..' is juxtaposed with Denzel Washington's image, implying that he embodies this role. His authoritative and respected public persona is used to represent the concept of being 'the loudest one in the room', creating an analogical mapping where the textual concept is projected onto the visual entity. This mapping is reinforced by his subtle, knowing expression, which conveys sarcasm or wisdom, suggesting he is commenting on or embodying the idea.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
